      "writtenOn": "2018-10-10T20:31:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "https://cs.corp.google.com/android/tools/tradefederation/core/res/config/suite/test_mapping_suite.xml?q\u003dtest_mapping_suite.xml\u0026dr\u0026l\u003d22\n\nWe do reboot between \"test modules\" not individual test methods, but I think modules is what you\u0027re asking for.\n\nB/C I work on developer tooling, I\u0027m not familiar enough to answer if that\u0027s enough to address Smoreland\u0027s concerns regarding selinux/sepolicy.\n\n\nThe thing I am more concerned with is that when you ran this through TreeHugger, the devices often stopped responding when running the teardown commands.... It seemed to be flakey if it would go offline or not but at a high enough flake rate that there\u0027s something going on.\n\n\nIf you need help launching a virtual gce cuttlefish device to reproduce the TH presubmit environment locally ping Kevcheng@ and I to help set you up with that.",
